  "fix": {
    "fix_type": "restructure",
    "target_module": "fir_filter",
    "added_latency_cycles": 0,
    "modified_rtl": "module fir_filter #(parameter N=8, parameter WIDTH=16) (\n    input clk, input rst, input en,\n    input  signed [WIDTH-1:0] sample_in,\n    output signed [WIDTH-1:0] sample_out\n);\nreg signed [WIDTH-1:0] c [N-1:0];\nreg signed [WIDTH-1:0] Q [N-1:0];\nreg signed [40:0] imm;\nreg signed [40:0] psum_lo;\nreg signed [40:0] psum_hi;\ninteger i, j, k;\n\nalways @(posedge clk) begin\n    if (rst) begin\n        for (i=0; i<N; i=i+1) begin\n \n            Q[i] <= 0;\n        end\n        c[0] <= 16'sd3;  c[1] <= 16'sd11;  c[2] <= 16'sd24;  c[3] <= 16'sd31;\n        c[4] <= 16'sd31; c[5] <= 16'sd24;  c[6] <= 16'sd11;  c[7] <= 16'sd3;\n    end else if (en) begin        // <-- only shift on a genuine new sample\n        Q[0] <= sample_in;\n        for (j=1; j<N; j=j+1)\n            Q[j] <= Q[j-1];\n    end\n    // else: hold \u2014 no new sample this cycle, don't shift\nend\n\n// Pipeline stage 1: two 4-product half-sums registered to split the MAC chain\n// Reduction rebalanced into a tree ((a+b)+(c+d)) instead of a serial\n// left-to-right chain, to shorten the combinational depth feeding the\n// psum_lo/psum_hi registers. Two's-complement addition is associative\n// modulo 2^n, so the regrouping is bit-exact identical to the original\n// serial sum for every input; only the internal gate depth changes.\nalways @(posedge clk) begin\n    if (rst) begin\n        psum_lo <= 0;\n        psum_hi <= 0;\n    end else begin\n        psum_lo <= ((c[0] * Q[0]) + (c[1] * Q[1])) + ((c[2] * Q[2]) + (c[3] * Q[3]));\n        psum_hi <= ((c[4] * Q[4]) + (c[5] * Q[5])) + ((c[6] * Q[6]) + (c[7] * Q[7]));\n    end\nend\n\n// Pipeline stage 2: final reduction (combinational, as before)\nalways @(*) begin\n    imm = psum_lo + psum_hi;\nend\nassign sample_out = imm[WIDTH-1:0];\nendmodule\n",
    "rationale": "The path runs from a Q[] shift-register DFF (line 13 block) through ~34 unattributed gates (the c[i]*Q[i] multipliers plus the serial +/+/+ reduction) into the psum_lo/psum_hi DFF (line 30 block). Retiming was rejected: there is no intermediate register anywhere inside this combinational MAC cloud to slide - Q[] and c[] are the only upstream registers and psum_lo/psum_hi the only downstream one, and moving either would change which pipeline stage samples the input, altering latency/function, not just its balance. Pipelining was rejected because it's strictly worse than available restructuring here: adding a stage would delay sample_out and force compensating delay on the reconvergent psum_lo/psum_hi-to-imm path and any external logic that also consumes sample latency, at added cost the restructure avoids entirely. NO_FIX was rejected because, even though 34/36 cells are unattributed, the RTL shown is the only plausible source of a 3-deep serial add chain of exactly this shape (four product terms summed left-to-right per stage-1 half), and it is directly editable.\n\nFix: RESTRUCTURE. In the stage-1 always block I rebalanced the serial 4-term sums `(c0*Q0)+(c1*Q1)+(c2*Q2)+(c3*Q3)` (3 sequential 32-bit adds) into a tree `((c0*Q0)+(c1*Q1)) + ((c2*Q2)+(c3*Q3))` (2 adds in parallel, then 1 final add), applied identically to both psum_lo and psum_hi so the two reconvergent halves stay balanced with each other and with the unchanged final-reduction stage. This removes one adder level (~2 stages of NOR2/OAI21-style carry logic) from the critical chain while leaving register count and cycle latency exactly as before (added_latency_cycles = 0). Since all operands are 32-bit self-determined products summed in 2's-complement arithmetic, addition is associative modulo 2^32 regardless of grouping, and the result is sign-extended identically into the 41-bit psum_lo/psum_hi target either way, so the produced value is bit-exact for every input - only the gate depth on the path changes, not the function.",
